    "words": [
      "custom-n",
      "tradition-n",
      "habit-n"
    ],
    "note": "A **habit** belongs to one person and is often done without thinking (*a habit of biting her nails*). A **custom** is shared by the people of a place or a group (*the custom of shaking hands*). A **tradition** is a custom or belief passed down from older people to younger ones over a long time (*a family tradition*)."
  },
  "usage_note": "**Customs**, always plural, is a different use: the place at a border where bags are checked (*go through customs*). See that entry.",
